Package: programmers-screenshot
Version: @VERSION@
Section: graphics
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: python3 (>= 3.8),
         python3-gi,
         python3-gi-cairo,
         python3-cairo,
         gir1.2-gtk-3.0,
         gir1.2-gdkpixbuf-2.0,
         gir1.2-notify-0.7,
         xclip | wl-clipboard
Recommends: gir1.2-wnck-3.0,
            nautilus | dolphin | nemo | thunar,
            gnome-session-canberra | pulseaudio-utils | pipewire-bin | alsa-utils
Maintainer: Shubshub
Homepage: https://github.com/shubshub/programmers-screenshot
Description: Minimal region screenshot tool for hotkey binding
 Freezes the screen and puts a toolbar across the top. Mark out a region,
 draw on it with the pen, then press Capture. The result is copied to the
 clipboard and saved as a timestamped PNG in ~/Pictures/Screenshots,
 with a shutter sound and a notification offering to open the image or
 show it in its folder.
 .
 Tools are pluggable: a new one is a single file plus a registry line.
 .
 Includes region, freehand pen, highlighter, line/rectangle/circle/arrow,
 measurement, colour picking, redaction, pixelation, numbered step and
 text tools.
 .
 It does one thing on one keypress: mark up, capture, done. No editor, no
 upload prompts, and nothing between the key and the overlay. Register a GNOME shortcut with --install-hotkey, or point any
 shortcut at the programmers-screenshot command.
 .
 A shot can also be described as JSON rather than taken by hand, so a
 script or an agent can produce documentation screenshots: a window or a
 region, a delay, and boxes, arrows, numbered steps, labels, redactions and
 pixelation. Off until switched on in the settings window.
 .
 Works on GNOME under X11 and Wayland, and spans multi-monitor layouts.
 Naming a window with --window needs X11 and gir1.2-wnck-3.0.
